{
  "root_cause": "The Datepicker class lacks a _onBlur method to handle blur events on the input field, and lacks a hide method to delegate to the picker. The blur event listener is registered but calls a non-existent method, so the datepicker does not hide when the user tabs away.",
  "repair_strategy": "Add a hide method to the Datepicker class that calls this.picker.hide(), and add an _onBlur method that conditionally calls this.update() based on the updateOnBlur config, then calls this.hide().",
  "edits": [
    {
      "path": "js/Datepicker.js",
      "sha256": "55bc634a806da095ca30921bdc0d463fdc2fd63dff3eeab32b3d673bab3ef609",
      "before": "  /**
   * Exit from edit mode
   * Not available on inline picker or when the picker element is hidden
   * @param  {Object} [options] - function options
   * - update: {boolean} - whether to call update() after exiting
   *     If false, input field is revert to the existing selection
   *     default: false
   */
  exitEditMode(options = undefined) {
    if (this.inline || !this.editMode) {
      return;
    }
    const opts = Object.assign({update: false}, options);
    delete this.editMode;
    this.inputField.classList.remove('in-edit');
    if (opts.update) {
      this.update(opts);
    }
  }
}
",
      "after": "  /**
   * Exit from edit mode
   * Not available on inline picker or when the picker element is hidden
   * @param  {Object} [options] - function options
   * - update: {boolean} - whether to call update() after exiting
   *     If false, input field is revert to the existing selection
   *     default: false
   */
  exitEditMode(options = undefined) {
    if (this.inline || !this.editMode) {
      return;
    }
    const opts = Object.assign({update: false}, options);
    delete this.editMode;
    this.inputField.classList.remove('in-edit');
    if (opts.update) {
      this.update(opts);
    }
  }

  /**
   * Hide the picker element
   */
  hide() {
    this.picker.hide();
  }

  /**
   * Handle blur event on the input field
   */
  _onBlur() {
    if (this.config.updateOnBlur) {
      this.update();
    }
    this.hide();
  }
}
"
    }
  ],
  "expected_accessibility_effect": "When the user tabs away from the date input field, the datepicker will close, ensuring that it does not obscure subsequent content and allowing assistive technologies to navigate the page correctly.",
  "functional_risks": [
    "Hiding the picker on blur may cause the picker to disappear if the user intends to interact with it via an assistive technology that simulates focus loss without actual user intent to leave the field.",
    "If the picker is made focusable in the future (e.g., by adding tabindex to its elements), the blur listener might hide it prematurely when navigating into the picker via keyboard."
  ],
  "verification_requirements": [
    "Tabbing away from the date input field with a valid date should update the form data and hide the datepicker.",
    "Tabbing away from the date input field with an invalid date (outside min/max) should hide the datepicker without updating the form data.",
    "Clicking on the datepicker buttons should not cause the picker to hide unexpectedly.",
    "The datepicker should still hide when clicking outside the picker (via the existing onClickOutside listener)."
  ]
}
